Title

ImpactIQ: AI-Powered Infrastructure Change Impact Analyzer

⸻

Introduction & Problem Description

In today’s IT environment, infrastructure is highly interconnected. Network devices such as routers, switches, and firewalls, along with other systems, depend on each other in complex ways. Because of this, even a small configuration change can have a wide and unexpected impact.

Currently, impact analysis before making a change is mostly manual and based on experience. Engineers rely on partial documentation, static diagrams, or past knowledge. There is no centralized system that clearly shows how a change in one component will affect other devices, network paths, or dependent services.

This leads to several challenges:
	•	Limited visibility of dependencies across the network
	•	Unexpected service impact after changes
	•	Increased incidents caused by small configuration updates
	•	Reactive troubleshooting instead of proactive planning

For example, a simple interface shutdown, ACL modification, or route update can unintentionally affect multiple downstream devices or business-critical services. These issues are often identified only after the change is implemented.

The core problem is the lack of visibility and prediction before executing infrastructure changes, especially in network environments.

⸻

Proposed Solution

We propose ImpactIQ, an AI-powered Infrastructure Change Impact Analyzer that helps engineers understand the impact of a change before it is applied.

The initial focus of ImpactIQ will be on network infrastructure such as routers, switches, and firewalls, with the ability to extend to broader IT systems in future phases.

The solution works in a simple and practical way:

First, ImpactIQ collects and analyzes infrastructure data including network configurations, topology, routing information, and telemetry. Using this data, it builds a dynamic dependency map that shows how devices, interfaces, and network paths are interconnected.

Next, when an engineer provides a planned change (such as interface shutdown, ACL update, route modification, or VLAN change), ImpactIQ simulates the change and analyzes how it will propagate across the network.

The system identifies:
	•	Affected devices and interfaces
	•	Downstream dependencies
	•	Potential service impact
	•	Extent of impact (blast radius)

An AI layer enhances this by learning from past changes and incidents to predict risk levels and improve accuracy over time.

Finally, ImpactIQ presents a clear and simple output including:
	•	Impacted components
	•	Risk level (Low / Medium / High)
	•	Impact path visibility
	•	Suggested precautions before execution

This enables engineers to make informed and confident decisions before applying any change.

⸻

Benefits and Impact

ImpactIQ provides strong and practical benefits for infrastructure and network operations:
	•	Reduced Incidents
By understanding impact in advance, teams can prevent outages caused by hidden dependencies
	•	Better Change Planning
Engineers can take informed decisions instead of relying on assumptions
	•	Improved Visibility
Clear understanding of how devices and services are interconnected
	•	Faster Troubleshooting
Dependency mapping helps quickly identify root causes when issues occur
	•	Increased Confidence in Changes
Teams can perform changes with greater certainty and reduced risk
	•	Scalable for Future Use
While initially focused on network infrastructure, the solution can be extended to servers, firewalls, and applications

Example:
If an engineer plans to shut down an interface on a core network device, ImpactIQ can show all dependent devices, affected paths, and associated services along with a risk level. This allows the engineer to plan mitigation steps or reschedule the change, avoiding potential outages.

⸻

Bottom Line

ImpactIQ acts as a pre-change intelligence layer for infrastructure operations, helping teams understand impact, reduce risk, and move from reactive issue handling to proactive and controlled change management.

